<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81352" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περι-ζώννυμι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gird upon</i> a person, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸ
				ξίφος [τινί</span>] <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				6.9.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Hann.</u>
				20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				40.460
			</span></i> (prob. l.); <i>gird</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
				παιδίον</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
			</span></i>inc.<i><span class="en">
				20.1
			</span></i> :—more freq. in 
				Med.
			 with pf.
			
				Pass.
			, <i>gird oneself with</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾤαν
				λουτρίδα</span> Theopomp. Com.<i><span class="en">
				37
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσθῆτα, τήβεννον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Rom.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cor.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυμνὸς ὢν τοῦτον τὸν ἄνδρα
				περιεζώσατο</span>
			<i>put</i> him <i>on</i> as a defence, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ᾽ ὑπόνοιαν</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίτροπον
				ἐποιήσατο</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				687
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιεζῶσθαι τὴν φορβειάν</span>
			<i>to have</i> their halter <i>girded round them.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1324b16
			</span></i>: c. dat., -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζώσασθαι τοῖς ἐντέροις τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.26
				</span></i>
			 W.:abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κλέων . . περιζωσάμενος ἐδημηγόρησε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					28.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. κοσμίως ἄνωθεν καὶ κάτωθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.70a
				</span></i>
			; of a cook, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιεζωσμένος</span>
			<i>with his apron on</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				174.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				41.12
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ νῆτται περιεζωσμέναι ἐπλινθοφόρουν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1148
				</span></i>
			; of athletes, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.44.1
			</span></i>; of a dancer, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.22.10
			</span></i>.</div>
